#. Tag: author
#: darkmatter.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid "<firstname>Jasem</firstname> <surname>Mutlaq</surname>"
msgstr "<firstname>Jasem</firstname> <surname>Mutlaq</surname>"

#. Tag: title
#: darkmatter.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Dark Matter</title>"
msgstr "<title>Dark Matter</title>"

#. Tag: primary
#: darkmatter.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Dark Matter</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>Dark Matter</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Scientists are now quite comfortable with the idea that 90% of the mass in "
"the universe is in a form of matter that cannot be seen."
msgstr ""
"Naučnici sada osjećaju komotno sa idejom da 90% od mase univerzuma je u "
"nekoj formi koja se ne moze vidjeti."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Despite comprehensive maps of the nearby universe that cover the spectrum "
"from radio to gamma rays, we are only able to account of 10% of the mass "
"that must be out there. As Bruce H. Margon, an astronomer at the University "
"of Washington, told the New York Times in 2001: <quote>It's a fairly "
"embarrassing situation to admit that we can't find 90 percent of the "
"universe.</quote>"
msgstr ""
"Unatoč sveobuhvatne kartama obližnjem svemiru koja pokrivaju spektar od "
"radija do gama zraka, mi smo samo u mogućnosti da se računa od 10% od mase "
"koja mora biti vani. Kao Bruce H. Margon, astronom na Sveučilištu u "
"Washingtonu, izjavio je za New York Times u 2001. godini: <quote> To je "
"prilično neugodna situacija za priznati da mi ne možemo naći 90 posto "
"svemira </quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The term given this <quote>missing mass</quote> is <firstterm>Dark Matter</"
"firstterm>, and those two words pretty well sum up everything we know about "
"it at this point. We know there is <quote>Matter</quote>, because we can see "
"the effects of its gravitational influence. However, the matter emits no "
"detectable electromagnetic radiation at all, hence it is <quote>Dark</"
"quote>. There exist several theories to account for the missing mass ranging "
"from exotic subatomic particles, to a population of isolated black holes, to "
"less exotic brown and white dwarfs. The term <quote>missing mass</quote> "
"might be misleading, since the mass itself is not missing, just its light. "
"But what is exactly dark matter and how do we really know it exists, if we "
"cannot see it?"
msgstr ""
"Pojam dat<quote>nestaloj masi </quote> jest <firstterm> tamna materija </"
"firstterm>, a te dvije riječi prilično dobro sažeti sve što znamo o tome u "
"ovom trenutku. Mi znamo da je <quote> Materija </quote>, jer možemo vidjeti "
"posljedice svog gravitacijskog utjecaja. Međutim, pitanje emitira nikakvu "
"mjerljivu elektromagnetsko zračenje na sve, stoga je <quote> Tamno </quote>. "
"Postoji nekoliko teorija na račun za nestalim mase u rasponu od egzotičnog "
"subatomskih čestica, u populaciji od izoliranih crnih rupa, manje egzotične "
"smeđe i bijeli patuljci.Izraz <quote> nestala masa </quote> moglo biti "
"pogrešno, jer sama masa nije nedostaje, samo svoju svjetlost. No, ono što je "
"točno tamna materija i kako zapravo znamo da postoji, ako je ne  možemo  "
"vidjeti?"

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The story began in 1933 when Astronomer Fritz Zwicky was studying the "
"motions of distant and massive clusters of galaxies, specifically the Coma "
"cluster and the Virgo cluster. Zwicky estimated the mass of each galaxy in "
"the cluster based on their luminosity, and added up all of the galaxy masses "
"to get a total cluster mass. He then made a second, independent estimate of "
"the cluster mass, based on measuring the spread in velocities of the "
"individual galaxies in the cluster. To his suprise, this second "
"<firstterm>dynamical mass</firstterm> estimate was <emphasis>400 times</"
"emphasis> larger than the estimate based on the galaxy light."
msgstr ""
"Priča je počela 1933. godine, kada Astronom Fritz Zwicky je proučavanje "
"kretanja udaljenih i masivnih klastera galaksija, posebno klastera Coma i "
"klastera Djevica. Zwicky procjenjuje masu svake galaksije u klasteru na "
"temelju njihove svjetlosti, i zbroji sve galaksije masa kako bi dobili "
"ukupnu masu klastera. On je tada napravio drugu, neovisnu procjenu klastera "
"mase, na temelju mjerenja širenje u brzinama pojedinih galaksija u klasteru. "
"Na njegovo iznenađenje, ovaj drugi <firstterm> dinamička masa </firstterm> "
"Procjena je <firstterm> 400 puta</firstterm> veći od procjena temeljena na "
"svjetlu galaksije."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Although the evidence was strong at Zwicky's time, it was not until the "
"1970s that scientists began to explore this discrepancy comprehensively. It "
"was at this time that the existence of Dark Matter began to be taken "
"seriously. The existence of such matter would not only resolve the mass "
"deficit in galaxy clusters; it would also have far more reaching "
"consequences for the evolution and fate of the universe itself."
msgstr ""
"Iako su dokazi bili jaki u Zwicky-jevo vrijeme, tek 1970-ih su naučnici "
"počeli istraživati tu neusklađenost sveobuhvatno. Stoga u ovom trenutku su "
"postojanje tamne materije počeli uzimati ozbiljno.Postojanje takve stvari ne "
"samo da će riješiti masovni deficit u galaktičkim klasterima; nego i šire "
"posljedice za razvoj i sudbinu samog svemira."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another phenomenon that suggested the need for dark matter is the rotational "
"curves of <firstterm>Spiral Galaxies</firstterm>. Spiral Galaxies contain a "
"large population of stars that orbit the Galactic center on nearly circular "
"orbits, much like planets orbit a star. Like planetary orbits, stars with "
"larger galactic orbits are expected to have slower orbital speeds (this is "
"just a statement of Kepler's 3rd Law). Actually, Kepler's 3rd Law only "
"applies to stars near the perimeter of a Spiral Galaxy, because it assumes "
"the mass enclosed by the orbit to be constant."
msgstr ""
"Još jedan fenomen koji je predložio potrebu za tamne materije jest okretna "
"krivulja <firstterm>spiralnih galaksija </firstterm>. Spiralne galaksije "
"sadrže veliku populaciju zvijezda koja kruže u galaktički centar na gotovo "
"kružnim orbitama, baš kao i planeta u orbiti oko zvijezde. Kao planetarnih "
"orbita, zvijezde s galaktički orbite se očekuje da će imati sporije "
"orbitalne brzine (to je samo izjava Keplerovog 3. Zakona). Zapravo, Keplerov "
"3. Zakona odnosi se samo na zvijezde blizu oboda spiralne galaksije, jer "
"pretpostavlja da ce  masa koja okruzuje  orbitu biti konstantna."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"However, astronomers have made observations of the orbital speeds of stars "
"in the outer parts of a large number of spiral galaxies, and none of them "
"follow Kepler's 3rd Law as expected. Instead of falling off at larger radii, "
"the orbital speeds remain remarkably constant. The implication is that the "
"mass enclosed by larger-radius orbits increases, even for stars that are "
"apparently near the edge of the galaxy. While they are near the edge of the "
"luminous part of the galaxy, the galaxy has a mass profile that apparently "
"continues well beyond the regions occupied by stars."
msgstr ""
"No, astronomi su napravili opažanja od orbitalne brzine zvijezda u vanjskim "
"dijelovima velikog broja spiralnih galaksija, i nitko od njih slijede "
"Keplerova 3. Zakona, kao što se očekivalo. Umjesto pada na većim radijusima, "
"orbitalna brzina i dalje izuzetno konstantan.Implikacija je da je masa "
"okružen većim radijusom orbite povećava, čak i za zvijezde koje su navodno "
"blizu ruba galaksije. Dok su oni u blizini ruba svjetlosnog dijela "
"galaksije, galaksija ima masu koja očito nastavlja i izvan područja koja su "
"okupirali zvijezde."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is another way to think about it: Consider the stars near the perimeter "
"of a spiral galaxy, with typical observed orbital velocities of 200 "
"kilometers per second. If the galaxy consisted of only the matter that we "
"can see, these stars would very quickly fly off from the galaxy, because "
"their orbital speeds are four times larger than the galaxy's escape "
"velocity. Since galaxies are not seen to be spinning apart, there must be "
"mass in the galaxy that we are not accounting for when we add up all the "
"parts we can see."
msgstr ""
"Tu je još jedan način da se razmisli o tome: Razmislite zvijezde u blizini "
"obodu spiralnoj galaksiji, s tipičnim promatranih orbitalnih brzina od 200 "
"kilometara u sekundi. Ako galaksija sastojala od samo stvari koja možemo "
"vidjeti, ta zvijezda će vrlo brzo odletjeti iz galaksije, jer su im "
"orbitalne brzine su četiri puta veći od galaksijinih brzina oslobađana. "
"Budući da galaksije nisu viđene da se vrte , mora postojati masa u galaksiji "
"koja nismo uracunali kada doamo sve dijelove koje vidimo."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Several theories have surfaced in literature to account for the missing mass "
"such as <acronym>WIMP</acronym>s (Weakly Interacting Massive Particles), "
"<acronym>MACHO</acronym>s (MAssive Compact Halo Objects), primordial black "
"holes, massive neutrinos, and others; each with their pros and cons. No "
"single theory has yet been accepted by the astronomical community, because "
"we so far lack the means to conclusively test one theory against the other."
msgstr ""
"Nekoliko teorije su se pojavile u književnosti na račun za nestalim mase, "
"kao što su <acronym>WIMP</acronym>s (Weakly Interacting Massive Particles), "
"<acronym>MACHO</acronym>s (MAssive Compact Halo Objects), primordijalnih "
"crnih rupa, masivne neutrine, i drugi; svaki sa svojim prednostima i "
"nedostacima. Niti jedna teorija još nije bio prihvaćen od strane astronomske "
"zajednice, jer smo do sada u  nedostaje sredstava za konačno testirati jednu "
"teoriju protiv drugoga."

#. Tag: para
#: darkmatter.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can see the galaxy clusters that Professor Zwicky studied to discover "
"Dark Matter. Use the &kstars; Find Object Window (<keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>) to center on <quote>M 87</quote> to "
"find the Virgo Cluster, and on <quote>NGC 4884</quote> to find the Coma "
"Cluster. You may have to zoom in to see the galaxies. Note that the Virgo "
"Cluster appears to be much larger on the sky. In reality, Coma is the larger "
"cluster; it only appears smaller because it is further away."
msgstr ""
"Možete vidjeti galaktičkih klastera koje je profesor Zwicky studirao za "
"otkrivanje tamne tvari. Koristite &kstars; Nađi Objekt Prozor  (<keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>)da se usredotočiei na "
"<quote> M 87 </quote> naći klaster Djevica, a na <quote> NGC 4884 </quote> "
"naći klaster Berenikine kose. Možda ćete morati zumirati da vidite "
"galaksije. Imajte na umu koja Djevica klastera, kako se čini puno veći na "
"nebu. U stvarnosti, Koma jest veća nakupina; samo se pojavi manji, jer je to "
"još daleko."
